# Create Component Workflow

## Component Creation Checklist

### 1. File Structure
- **Location**: `src/components/<domain>/` for dumb, props-based UI
  (`auth/`, `calls/`, `conversations/`, `groups/`, `messages/`, `music-rooms/`,
  `notifications/`, `profile/`, `songs/`, `stories/`), `src/components/common/`
  for cross-domain dumb primitives, `src/components/mui/` for MUI wrappers
  (see [[create-mui-wrapper]]).
- **Naming**: PascalCase, `.jsx` extension — one component per file, file name
  matches the default export (see the project's naming rules). A `Component`
  suffix is used for MUI wrappers under `components/mui/`; domain components
  don't need the suffix (`MessageBubble.jsx`, not `MessageBubbleComponent.jsx`).
- **Pattern**: Components are props-based only, **no business logic** — no
  `fetch`/RTK Query hook calls, no `useSelector`/`useDispatch`. Data and
  callbacks come from the matching container in
  `src/features/containers/<domain>/`.

### 2. Component Template
```javascript
// src/components/messages/MessageBubble.jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react'
import { Box, Typography, Avatar } from '@mui/material'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

// Component scope
const BUBBLE_MAX_WIDTH = '70%'

const MessageBubble = ({
  message,
  isOwnMessage,
  showAvatar = true
}) => {
  // States, refs, selectors, RTK Query hooks
  // (None for this component - it's props-based only)

  // useEffect hooks
  // (None for this component)

  // Other functions and logic
  const formatTimestamp = (isoString) => {
    return new Date(isoString).toLocaleTimeString([], {
      hour: '2-digit',
      minute: '2-digit'
    })
  }

  // Return/rendering
  return (
    <Box
      sx={{
        display: 'flex',
        flexDirection: isOwnMessage ? 'row-reverse' : 'row',
        alignItems: 'flex-end',
        gap: 1,
        mb: 1
      }}
    >
      {showAvatar && !isOwnMessage && (
        <Avatar src={message.sender.avatarUrl} sx={{ width: 28, height: 28 }} />
      )}

      <Box
        sx={{
          maxWidth: BUBBLE_MAX_WIDTH,
          px: 1.5,
          py: 1,
          borderRadius: 2,
          bgcolor: isOwnMessage ? 'primary.main' : 'background.paper',
          color: isOwnMessage ? 'primary.contrastText' : 'text.primary'
        }}
      >
        <Typography variant="body2">{message.content}</Typography>

        <Typography
          variant="caption"
          sx={{ display: 'block', mt: 0.5, opacity: 0.7 }}
        >
          {formatTimestamp(message.createdAt)}
        </Typography>
      </Box>
    </Box>
  )
}

MessageBubble.propTypes = {
  message: PropTypes.shape({
    id: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
    content: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
    createdAt: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
    sender: PropTypes.shape({
      id: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
      displayName: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
      avatarUrl: PropTypes.string
    }).isRequired
  }).isRequired,
  isOwnMessage: PropTypes.bool.isRequired,
  showAvatar: PropTypes.bool
}

export default memo(MessageBubble)
```

> Note on PropTypes: `prop-types` is not currently in `package.json` — verify
> it's actually installed before writing `PropTypes.shape(...)` blocks like
> the one above; if it isn't installed yet, that's a gap to flag, not silently
> work around.

### 3. Music Room Component Example
```javascript
// src/components/music-rooms/RoomMemberCard.jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react'
import { Card, CardContent, Typography, Avatar, Box } from '@mui/material'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

const RoomMemberCard = ({
  member,
  isDj = false,
  isSpeaking = false
}) => {
  return (
    <Card
      sx={{
        display: 'flex',
        alignItems: 'center',
        gap: 1.5,
        p: 1.5,
        borderRadius: 2,
        border: isDj ? '2px solid' : '1px solid',
        borderColor: isDj ? 'primary.main' : 'divider',
        transition: 'all 0.2s ease-in-out'
      }}
    >
      <Avatar
        src={member.avatarUrl}
        sx={{
          width: 40,
          height: 40,
          outline: isSpeaking ? '2px solid' : 'none',
          outlineColor: 'success.main'
        }}
      />

      <CardContent sx={{ p: '0 !important' }}>
        <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ fontWeight: isDj ? 600 : 400 }}>
          {member.displayName}
        </Typography>

        {isDj && (
          <Typography variant="caption" color="primary.main">
            DJ
          </Typography>
        )}
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
  )
}

RoomMemberCard.propTypes = {
  member: PropTypes.shape({
    id: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
    displayName: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
    avatarUrl: PropTypes.string
  }).isRequired,
  isDj: PropTypes.bool,
  isSpeaking: PropTypes.bool
}

export default memo(RoomMemberCard)
```

### 4. Component Requirements Checklist

#### ✅ Basic Requirements
- [ ] Use functional component with hooks only
- [ ] Add React.memo for performance
- [ ] Include PropTypes with proper validation (once `prop-types` is
      installed — verify via `package.json`)
- [ ] Provide default values via destructured default parameters, not
      `Component.defaultProps` (deprecated for function components)
- [ ] Use absolute imports once the alias is configured (see the
      architecture rules — `resolve.alias`/`jsconfig.json` don't exist yet)
- [ ] Keep component under 300 lines

#### ✅ MUI Integration
- [ ] Use MUI components as base
- [ ] Apply consistent styling with SX prop only — no Tailwind classes,
      no inline `style` objects
- [ ] Include proper theme integration once `src/theme/index.js` exists
- [ ] Add hover and focus states with SX
- [ ] Ensure accessibility (ARIA labels, roles)
- [ ] Use MUI's responsive breakpoint system

#### ✅ Rhynk Specific
- [ ] No DJ-only music-room controls rendered for non-DJ members (hide, don't
      just disable) — but remember this is UX only, the server enforces it
- [ ] Handle empty/loading states gracefully for lists (conversations,
      messages, queue) since these components receive already-fetched data
- [ ] Consider mobile responsiveness with MUI breakpoints
- [ ] Include proper data validation for props (message/room/song shapes)

#### ✅ Testing
No test runner (Vitest/Jest) is configured in this repo yet — treat the
template below as the target shape once one is introduced, not as something
that runs today.
- [ ] Create test file: `__tests__/ComponentName.test.jsx`
- [ ] Test rendering with different props
- [ ] Test user interactions (clicks, hovers)
- [ ] Test accessibility compliance
- [ ] Test edge cases and error states

### 5. Test Template
```javascript
// src/components/messages/__tests__/MessageBubble.test.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react'
import MessageBubble from '../MessageBubble'

const mockMessage = {
  id: 'msg-1',
  content: 'Hey, check out this track!',
  createdAt: '2026-07-12T10:00:00.000Z',
  sender: {
    id: 'user-1',
    displayName: 'Nova',
    avatarUrl: null
  }
}

describe('MessageBubble', () => {
  it('renders message content correctly', () => {
    render(<MessageBubble message={mockMessage} isOwnMessage={false} />)

    expect(screen.getByText('Hey, check out this track!')).toBeInTheDocument()
  })

  it('aligns own messages to the right', () => {
    render(<MessageBubble message={mockMessage} isOwnMessage={true} />)

    expect(screen.getByText(mockMessage.content)).toBeInTheDocument()
  })
})
```

### 6. Common Component Types

#### Form Components
- `AppTextField` - Enhanced MUI TextField
- `AppSelect` - Enhanced MUI Select
- `AppCheckbox` - Enhanced MUI Checkbox
- `AppRadioGroup` - Enhanced MUI RadioGroup

#### Display Components
- `PresenceDot` - Online/away/offline indicator
- `TypingIndicator` - "X is typing…" display
- `TimestampDisplay` - Formatted relative time display
- `LoadingSpinner` - Consistent loading indicator

#### Layout Components
- `AppCard` - Standardized card component
- `AppModal` - Standardized modal component
- `AppDialog` - Standardized dialog component
- `AppTooltip` - Standardized tooltip component

#### Rhynk Domain Components
- `MessageBubble` - Single chat message display
- `RoomMemberCard` - Music-room member/DJ display
- `SongQueueItem` - Queued track row in a music room
- `StoryRing` - Story avatar with unseen/seen ring state

### 7. Export Pattern
```javascript
// src/components/common/index.js
export { default as AppButton } from './AppButton'
export { default as AppTextField } from './AppTextField'
export { default as AppCard } from './AppCard'
export { default as AppModal } from './AppModal'

// Usage
import { AppButton, AppTextField } from 'components/common'
```
